Everybody (who doesn't have a killfile...) knows my Sporkhack Rogue
Chinese Fire Drill by now,  go get a wish and get Magicbane first and
then see to armor afterwards.

Due to sac gifted orc mail (poly potioned to studs thanks...) I
figured I was fairly well setup for armor and so wished for the
spellcaster's Helm (also got sac gifted a tight cloak, so spells can
wait) and I'm down in the middle of the quest poking things with
Magicbane (found it in a bones file, oddly common on my local system
and Spork isn't supported for trading bones yet) when i run into an
Orange dragon (yes, PFSC firmly in place, huh?) so I scale it and
enchant it up.

And suddenly I have a new favorite armor (even if it means I have to
keep the Sokoban amulet).

Why do I want a rogue in orange?  It's a status thing.  Magicbane is
very good at putting a lot of negative statuses on critters, but one
thing it doesn't do is slow.

So Magicbane does scare (one way or another) and the target gets
slowed by my armor so I can drop in multiple (status inflicting)
backstabs.  Needless to say the Master Assassin didn't last very long.

I think I'll run this game to the end to see how well this armor does
against riders.

